From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:11:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: wire the igloo bridge device into the build

Adds CONFIG_IGLOO_BRIDGE (default y) and compiles
src/hw/misc/igloo_bridge.c, the host end of a TCP stream bridge that an
in-guest igloo kernel module drives over one Penguin hypercall. It stands
in for vsock on guest kernels that cannot have AF_VSOCK (before 3.9, or
with no virtio transport): "-device igloo-bridge,fwd=...,ctl=..." exposes
host port forwards into the guest and a unix control socket with the
vhost-user-vsock style "CONNECT <port>" handshake.

The wire protocol is src/include/hw/misc/igloo_bridge_proto.h, shared
verbatim with the guest module. The device takes Penguin's single guest
hypercall callback, so it is for runs without Penguin attached; under
Penguin the same protocol is served by a plugin.
---
 hw/misc/Kconfig     | 4 ++++
 hw/misc/meson.build | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/Kconfig b/hw/misc/Kconfig
index 1543ee66531bfcbba8293c8580798cb08c9cbd09..f2bc5dbe8c5f4891d331107bdfd79dffed82c6bf 100644
--- a/hw/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/hw/misc/Kconfig
@@ -258,3 +258,7 @@ config XLNX_ZYNQ_DDRC
     bool
 
 source macio/Kconfig
+
+config IGLOO_BRIDGE
+    bool
+    default y
diff --git a/hw/misc/meson.build b/hw/misc/meson.build
index 23265f6035bd566f4f301d8b5f59349255ff3e06..b757e718056da95b3b6b42688dccf27334915624 100644
--- a/hw/misc/meson.build
+++ b/hw/misc/meson.build
@@ -168,3 +168,5 @@ system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_SBSA_REF', if_true: files('sbsa_ec.c'))
 
 # HPPA devices
 system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_LASI', if_true: files('lasi.c'))
+
+system_ss.add(when: 'CONFIG_IGLOO_BRIDGE', if_true: files('igloo_bridge.c'))
